  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Fix native and TileLang edge candidates that discard tangential separation, and require both reconstructed contact witnesses to lie in their shapes.",
  "regressions": [
    "Keep the full 343-pair PFM corpus. Cone/capsule, capsule/cone, cylinder/capsule and cylinder/cylinder cases retain valid GJK/EPA contacts and no longer emit invalid edge candidates.",
    "Add 24 explicit edge-witness cases covering parallel and reversed invalid edges, valid conformal and crossing contacts, both output frames, and scales 0.001, 1 and 1000.",
    "Replace the absolute 2D segment denominator threshold with a scale-relative determinant and Cramer evaluation so small perpendicular segments retain their crossing.",
    "Require independent containment of both polygonal features and both convex shapes, even if native and target outputs match. Inject the original capsule/cone failure in a corruption test.",
    "Preserve exact counts, IDs, readonly storage and guards; keep the original numerical output tolerance.",
    "Map registered general/joint restart operations to their shared scene shader modules and audit the actual workspace registry in addition to synthetic inventory tests."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "This is a paired reference correctness fix. Edge candidates are accepted only when their implicit second witness agrees with the computed second point within 32 f32 epsilon times coordinate scale.",
    "Filtering an invalid clipped point preserves the existing valid GJK/EPA fallback; it does not add host collision computation or change contact prediction.",
    "Zero-distance CFM classification, production runtime integration and Ascend hardware qualification remain separate work."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0045-epa-degenerate-normal",
    "0046-convex-pfm-manifolds",
    "0052-connected-general-scenes"
  ]
